You have Fuchs endothelial dystrophy. This condition affects the inner layer of cells on the cornea called endothelial cells. These cells normally pump fluid out of the cornea to keep it clear.\
\
When these cells gradually decline in number, fluid can accumulate within the cornea. This can cause blurred vision, glare, and hazy vision, especially in the morning when the eyes first open.\
\
